Improved Cross-Referencing for User Feedback Interpretation
Sarah encountered a critical issue where 'better reporting' from sales was misinterpreted due to disparate definitions across different feedback sources (sales, support tickets). This led to building the wrong feature (e.g., 'scheduled exports' instead of 'dashboard sharing' or 'CSV downloads'). She needs a mechanism to cross-reference feedback sources to accurately understand user needs and avoid misinterpretations.

“Last week our top request from sales was "better reporting."”
“When I dug into support tickets, the word "report" meant three different things: scheduled exports, dashboard sharing, and CSV downloads.”
“We built the wrong one because nobody cross-referenced the sources.”
